{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BringCone","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BringCone","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Quaternion","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":51,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.normSq_hopf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.normSq_hopf","kind":"theorem","line":513,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L513-L518","doc":"The Hopf image has norm `normSq p ^ 2`, so it is a pure unit when `p` is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.re_hopf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.re_hopf","kind":"theorem","line":509,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L509-L511","doc":"The Hopf image `p·i·p̄` is pure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.chiralGammaU_eigen_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.chiralGammaU_eigen_iff","kind":"theorem","line":483,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L483-L507","doc":"**A radial direction is a chirality eigenvector only at its Hopf image.** For\na unit vector `p`, `Γ_u p = −p` iff `u = p·i·p̄`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.normSq_intertwiner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.normSq_intertwiner","kind":"theorem","line":474,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L474-L481","doc":"For pure units `u`, `v`, `normSq (1 − v·u) = 2·(1 + u·v)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.leftMul_star_leftMul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.leftMul_star_leftMul","kind":"theorem","line":468,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L468-L472","doc":"`L_{q̄} ∘ L_q = normSq q • id`: `L_q` is invertible when `normSq q` is a unit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.leftMul_intertwines_chiralGammaU","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.leftMul_intertwines_chiralGammaU","kind":"theorem","line":460,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L460-L466","doc":"`L_q`, which commutes with the Reeb triad, carries `Γ_u` to `Γ_v`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.intertwiner_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.intertwiner_mul","kind":"theorem","line":454,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L454-L458","doc":"For two square roots of `−1`, `q = 1 − v·u` satisfies `q·u = v·q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.chiralGammaU_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.chiralGammaU_neg","kind":"theorem","line":449,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L449-L452","doc":"**The antipodal unit is the global flip**: `Γ_{−u} = −Γ_u`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.chiralGammaU_anticomm_reebM_k","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.chiralGammaU_anticomm_reebM_k","kind":"theorem","line":442,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L442-L447","doc":"`M_k` anticommutes with `Γ_u`, for every `u`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.chiralGammaU_anticomm_reebM_j","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.chiralGammaU_anticomm_reebM_j","kind":"theorem","line":435,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L435-L440","doc":"`M_j` anticommutes with `Γ_u`, for every `u`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.chiralGammaU_comm_reebM_i","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.chiralGammaU_comm_reebM_i","kind":"theorem","line":430,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L430-L433","doc":"`M_i` commutes with `Γ_u`, for every `u`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.chiralGammaU_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.chiralGammaU_sq","kind":"theorem","line":422,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L422-L428","doc":"`Γ_u` is a grading for every complex-structure `u`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.re_eq_zero_of_sq_eq_neg_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.re_eq_zero_of_sq_eq_neg_one","kind":"theorem","line":398,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L398-L420","doc":"**Every square root of `−1` is pure**, over a domain of characteristic `≠ 2` in\nwhich `−1` is not a square. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.sq_eq_neg_one_iff_normSq_of_pure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.sq_eq_neg_one_iff_normSq_of_pure","kind":"theorem","line":381,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L381-L396","doc":"For a pure `u`, `u * u = −1` iff `normSq u = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.leftMul_complex_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.leftMul_complex_iff","kind":"theorem","line":371,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L371-L379","doc":"**`L_u` is a complex structure iff `u * u = −1`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.chiralGammaU_i","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.chiralGammaU_i","kind":"theorem","line":367,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L367-L369","doc":"`Γ_i` is the grading `chiralGamma` of the earlier section. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.chiralGammaU","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.chiralGammaU","kind":"def","line":363,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L363-L365","doc":"The chirality grading built from an arbitrary left unit: `Γ_u = L_u ∘ M_i`,\n`p ↦ u · p · i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.reebM_i_eq_mul_unitI","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.reebM_i_eq_mul_unitI","kind":"theorem","line":361,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L361-L361","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.unitI_mul_neg_unitI","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.unitI_mul_neg_unitI","kind":"theorem","line":358,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L358-L359","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.unitI_mul_unitI","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.unitI_mul_unitI","kind":"theorem","line":355,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L355-L356","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.unitJ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.unitJ","kind":"def","line":350,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L350-L353","doc":"The quaternionic unit `j` on the cone. Shared by `BringConeGauge` and\n`BringConeIcosahedral`, which each declared their own copy until both were imported\ntogether and the library root failed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.unitI","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.unitI","kind":"def","line":347,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L347-L348","doc":"The quaternionic unit `i` on the cone, named so that proofs can manipulate it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.commutes_reeb_triad_iff_leftMul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.commutes_reeb_triad_iff_leftMul","kind":"theorem","line":288,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L288-L305","doc":"**The commutant of the Reeb triad is the left multiplications.** An `R`-linear\nmap commuting with `M_i`, `M_j`, `M_k` is left multiplication by `f 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.leftI_eq_leftMul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.leftI_eq_leftMul","kind":"theorem","line":285,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L285-L286","doc":"`leftI` is the left multiplication by `i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.leftMul_comm_reebM_k","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.leftMul_comm_reebM_k","kind":"theorem","line":281,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L281-L283","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.leftMul_comm_reebM_j","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.leftMul_comm_reebM_j","kind":"theorem","line":277,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L277-L279","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.leftMul_comm_reebM_i","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.leftMul_comm_reebM_i","kind":"theorem","line":273,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L273-L275","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.leftMul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.leftMul","kind":"def","line":270,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L270-L271","doc":"Left multiplication by `u`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.reebM_j_ray_free","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.reebM_j_ray_free","kind":"theorem","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L232-L246","doc":"**`M_j` has no eigen-ray**: if `p * j = c • p` with `p ≠ 0`, then `c² + 1 = 0`.\nSo whenever `−1` is not a square in `R` and scalars cancel on the cone, `M_j`\nfixes no state, and it is a fixed-point-free involution on rays (its square is\nthe scalar `−1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.neg_eq_unit_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.neg_eq_unit_smul","kind":"theorem","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L226-L230","doc":"**Negation is a scalar**, `−p = (−1) • p`, so on rays (states) it is trivial\nand fixes every state. This retires `reebM_x² = −id` as the candidate `ι` on\nstates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.reebM_j_flips_eigen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.reebM_j_flips_eigen","kind":"theorem","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L219-L224","doc":"`M_j` sends a `Γ = −1` vector to a `Γ = +1` vector. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.chiralGamma_anticomm_reebM_j","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.chiralGamma_anticomm_reebM_j","kind":"theorem","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L213-L217","doc":"**`M_j` anticommutes with the grading**: it exchanges the two chiralities. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.chiralGamma_comm_reebM_i","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.chiralGamma_comm_reebM_i","kind":"theorem","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L207-L211","doc":"`M_i` commutes with the grading. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.chiralGamma_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.chiralGamma_sq","kind":"theorem","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L202-L205","doc":"**`Γ² = id`** — a grading, not a complex structure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.chiralGamma_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.chiralGamma_apply","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L196-L200","doc":"**`Γ` explicitly:** `−1` on the `1, i` components, `+1` on the `j, k` components. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.chiralGamma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.chiralGamma","kind":"def","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L193-L194","doc":"The chirality grading `Γ = L_i ∘ M_i`, i.e. `p ↦ i · p · i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.leftI","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.leftI","kind":"def","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L189-L191","doc":"Left multiplication by `i` — the second complex structure, commuting with every\nright multiplication (associativity). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.neg_free_of_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.neg_free_of_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L129-L139","doc":"**Negation is fixed-point free away from the origin**, whenever `2` is\ncancellable on the cone — which is exactly V10's `free_of_reeb_odd_grading`\nhypothesis, so a globally odd chirality grading exists on the punctured cone.\n\nThe hypothesis is an explicit cancellation property rather than a typeclass, so\nthe lemma stays over generic `[CommRing R]` per §7c. It holds in any `R` of\ncharacteristic `≠ 2` without zero divisors, and in particular in `ℝ` for the\narchimedean specialisation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.neg_fixed_iff_add_self_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.neg_fixed_iff_add_self_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L124-L127","doc":"**A fixed point of negation is exactly a solution of `p + p = 0`.**  Stated\nas an iff so the next lemma's hypothesis is visibly the only thing needed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.neg_involutive_cone","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.neg_involutive_cone","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L120-L122","doc":"**Negation on the cone is an involution** — the `ξ ↦ −ξ` of\n`archimedean-chirality`, as a map on the cone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.reebM_i_quartic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.reebM_i_quartic","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L113-L118","doc":"Each Reeb operator has **order four**, not two: its square is negation and\nits fourth power is the identity. So `M_i` itself is not the involution — its\nsquare is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.reebM_k_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.reebM_k_sq","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L108-L111","doc":"**`M_k² = −id`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.reebM_j_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.reebM_j_sq","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L103-L106","doc":"**`M_j² = −id`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.reebM_i_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.reebM_i_sq","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L97-L101","doc":"**`M_i² = −id`.**  Right-multiplication by `i` twice is negation, since\n`i² = −1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.reeb_twist_ki","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.reeb_twist_ki","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L59-L63","doc":"Quaternionic twist `[M_k, M_i] = 2·M_j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.reeb_twist_jk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.reeb_twist_jk","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L53-L57","doc":"Quaternionic twist `[M_j, M_k] = 2·M_i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.reeb_twist_ij","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.reeb_twist_ij","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L47-L51","doc":"Quaternionic twist `[M_i, M_j] = 2·M_k`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:lem:bring-cone-reeb-quaternionic-twist","label":"lem:bring-cone-reeb-quaternionic-twist","md":"quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/bring-cone-reeb-quaternionic-twist.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.reebM_k","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.reebM_k","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L44-L45","doc":"Reeb operator `M_k` — right-multiplication by the quaternionic unit `k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.reebM_j","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.reebM_j","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L42-L43","doc":"Reeb operator `M_j` — right-multiplication by the quaternionic unit `j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.reebM_i","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.reebM_i","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L40-L41","doc":"Reeb operator `M_i` — right-multiplication by the quaternionic unit `i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.BringCone","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.BringCone","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringCone.lean#L37-L38","doc":"The tetraplectic Bring cone, modelled on the quaternions over `R`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:bring-cone-tetraplectic-structure","label":"def:bring-cone-tetraplectic-structure","md":"quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/bring-cone-tetraplectic-structure.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}